    "text": "I recorded the diagnosis for incident 2 as `platform_resources`, with 0.6 confidence. The intake task's pod was killed for running out of memory, not because of the vendor's data.\n\n- **What failed:** In `intake__healthcare__eligibility`, run `manual__2026-10-21T13:00:00+00:00`, the `intake` task failed and `transform` was `upstream_failed`.\n- **Evidence for the cause:** The task log says \"return code -9 (SIGKILL): the pod was OOMKilled\".\n- **Why confidence is only 0.6:** The Kubernetes events returned no termination for the intake pod, so the OOM rests on the task log alone. The dbt test lookup for this feed also returned an internal error, so I had no test evidence either way.\n- **Separate open problem:** The feed's one quarantined file (`elig_20261020.csv`, quarantine id 1) is missing the `member_id` column and has `patient_ref` instead. That is a vendor contract problem and I did not link it to the failed run. I did not list quarantine ids, because the cause is not quarantined records.\n\nI also recorded five proposed steps from runbook `10-oomkilled` for a person to take. They start by confirming the OOM on the pod, since the events did not show it. They then cover the memory limit, a rerun of the intake task, and handling the quarantine on its own. Nothing was run.",
